{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Harhev</b> — an expression of command, like <b>har'ef va'agidah lekha</b>. And <b>tekhabbesheni</b> may be a verb, like <b>lekhabbesheni</b>, or <b>harhev</b> may be a noun like <b>harbeh</b>, and <b>tekhabbesheni</b> an imperative. Behold, he likened the soul that has become defiled to doing what is not proper, like something filthy that requires washing and purification."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 51, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:29.819857277Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}